Simon Jensen wrote:

> I had problems getting my Mylex DAC960 (PD I think) to work under RedHat
> 7.1... So i dropped getting it to work, and installed the drives on another
> scsi controller without RAID capabilities.
> Is there any easy way to get this controller to work. I would prefer to have
> "/" on a RAID partition to increase performance.

Was the error along the lines of a panic when root could not be mounted? 
  If so, you've been bit by the fact that the kernel needs help mapping 
a logical device name (e.g. /dev/sdaX) to the physical device major + 
minor number.  I opened a Bugzilla issue with RedHat about this last 
year.  Not sure if the underlying issue was ever fixed, but the 
workaround is to specify the root device in the form XXYY, where 'XX' is 
the major device number and 'YY' the minor - both in hexadecimal format.

Example: If your root is intended to be on /rd/c0d0p3, you would specify 
root=3003 to Grub (or, more likely, lilo).  In lilo, I think this needs 
to look like append="root=3003", but it's been a while and I'm fuzzy on 
the syntax.

See RH Bugzilla Issue #65207 for the entire thread.  Alternately, you 
can patch the kernel such that init recognizes the Mylex device files 
directly (see attached).

Steve



